join "Mama Zulu" left
join Hope (Neutral) right
Mama Zulu\: Three people have said the same thing in this room in a fortnight, which is more than usual.
- Said what?
	Hope: Said what?
	Mama Zulu\: That when the water committee is formed there will need to be someone to hold it. And then, both times, a pause. And then Naledi's name.
	Mama Zulu\: Nobody has said it to her. That is the part I find interesting.
	- Why not?
		Hope: Why not?
		Mama Zulu\: Because she would say no, and then she would be a person who has said no, and it would be harder the second time.
		Mama Zulu\: So they are saying it to each other first, until there are enough of them that it stops being a question.
		Mama Zulu\: That is how this village decides things. Slowly, and then all at once, and never in a meeting.
	- Who said it?
		Hope: Who said it?
		Mama Zulu\: People who were here.
		Mama Zulu\: I do not carry names out of this room. I carry the shape of a thing, and the shape of this one is that it is going to happen.
set {GameState.leadership_talk_established} = true